            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The data represents the airport in Zurich (uniqueairport) and is based on assumptions as follows: \nFoundation layer: 40 cm gravel and a life span of 100 years.\nConcrete floor: 22 cm with a concrete reinforcement of 1.8 kg steel/m2. and a lifespan of 30 years  .\nTransport distance 25 km.\nFor material and energy consumption due to the construction and disposal of buildings we employed generic modules as available from [Kellenberger, 2003 #94]. In order to facilitate a first estimate we made the assumptions as follows:\n· 70% of the built up area is occupied with building halls \n· 30% are multi storey buildings with an average of 5 floors. The assumed height between the floors is 2 .7m\n\n;
UUID: a86b716d-de3e-3d0d-8813-d4d53a8774be</common:generalComment>
